                  <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm mb-1">1. Cu Chi Tunnels + Cao Dai Great Temple (Tay Ninh)</div>
                  <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                    <strong>Logistics: Natural geographic synergy.</strong> Tay Ninh lies about 50 kilometers further northwest along Highway 22 toward the Cambodian border. You leave Saigon early, visit Cu Chi in the morning, continue to the kaleidoscopic Cao Dai Great Temple in time for the daily 12:00 PM midday prayer ceremony, enjoy lunch, and drive back to town in the late afternoon. Expect about 5 to 6 hours of total seat time, but it makes for an unforgettable full-day cultural dive.
